<BaseLayout title="How we rank PC hardware" description="How Core & Pixel reports comparable CPU and GPU benchmarks, explains limitations and shows separate US and Spain price snapshots." breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'How We Rank' }]} noindex>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'How We Rank' }]} />
  <section class="page-hero"><p class="kicker">Evidence and corrections</p><h1>How we rank PC hardware</h1><p>Rankings should help readers understand the evidence, not hide it behind a single unexplained score.</p></section>
  <div class="content-narrow prose">
    <h2>Keep unlike tests separate</h2><p>Gaming, productivity and value answer different questions. CPU gaming scores do not predict every productivity app. GPU results also depend on resolution, rendering method, game, settings and test system. We do not combine incompatible tests into one universal number.</p>
    <h2>Report the source’s results, not our own lab tests</h2><p>The current <a href="/cpus/performance-rankings/">CPU ranking</a> reports selected scores from Tom’s Hardware’s CPU hierarchy, last updated October 5, 2026. Its gaming index and multithreaded application index remain separate. The <a href="/gpus/performance-rankings/">GPU ranking</a> reports selected rasterization and ray-tracing indices from Tom’s Hardware’s GPU hierarchy, last updated June 24, 2026; its resolution-specific results remain separate. We link to the original test details and preserve the published index rather than averaging scores from different review labs.</p>
    <h2>Make test conditions visible</h2><p>Every benchmark section names its source and update date. The CPU gaming figures are a 1080p relative index; the GPU tables show relative indices at 1080p, 1440p and 4K. A higher percentage only describes the source’s test suite and conditions. It is not a guaranteed frame rate or a result for every game.</p>
    <h2>Use user-submitted scores carefully</h2><p>User-submitted benchmark databases can provide supplementary context. They are not the sole basis for our editorial rankings because systems, workloads and settings may not be controlled or directly comparable.</p>
    <h2>Show prices by market</h2><p>US prices use USD retailer examples. Spain prices use euro listings from Spanish retailers. The current CPU page pairs US price references reported with the October 5 hierarchy update and Spanish listings checked October 11, 2026. The GPU page uses US price checks dated October 8 and Spanish listings checked October 11, 2026. Listings can refer to different board-partner models and may change quickly. We do not convert US prices into euros, and price examples are not market-wide averages.</p>
    <h2>Update with a reason</h2><p>When evidence, price or availability changes, the page should state what changed and when it was checked. We do not change dates merely to make a page appear fresh. Readers can use the contact page to report an error; verified corrections will be recorded here.</p>
    <div class="draft-banner">Methodology draft: rankings and prices are editorial snapshots for owner review. Review source selection, update cadence and correction contact before publication. These pages remain noindex while under review.</div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
